[187|]{id|category|key|content|file|tags|date|ttl|accessed|links}:
  4968d360|knowledge|embed-minimap-fullscreen-bug|Bug minimap del demo (docs/public/viewer/embed.html, generado por scripts/generate-embed.mjs): se bugueaba al entrar en pantalla completa en el modal del home. Causa: (1) el handler de zoom NO llamaba updateMinimap() (el producto src/viewer/html.ts:483 sí) → el rectángulo del viewport quedaba stale al hacer zoom; (2) el embed no escuchaba window.resize → al fullscreenear el modal (CSS .viewer-modal:fullscreen .viewer-modal-frame height:100vh, docs/src/styles/home.css:823) el iframe redimensiona y el minimap + centro del grafo quedaban desincronizados. Fix: updateMinimap() en el zoom + window.addEventListener('resize') debounced (80ms) que llama resize() (recentra force center + sim restart) y updateMinimap(). switchTab ya llamaba graph.resize() (linea 432 del generador).||viewer;minimap;fullscreen;embed;bug|2026-07-31||1||0.77|1|2026-08-01T04:05:28.632Z
  2d299473|decision|graph-single-component-bridge|buildGraph (src/lib/graph.ts) ahora garantiza UN único componente conectado: tras el orphan fallback (orphanScore = tags*4 + key*2 + content, tie-break por key), un segundo pase calcula connectedComponents y puentea cada isla a la componente más grande con el par (a,b) de mayor orphanScore. generate-embed.mjs lo espeja EXACTO (fix: antes usaba un `deg` obsoleto en el orphan pass que conectaba el grafo por accidente — ahora usa adjMap en vivo + componente-bridge). Verificado: data.toon migrado (185 entries, 3 multilíneas reconstruidas: release-roadmap-post-engram, engram-features-implemented, mcp-apps-extensions-init-handler) → 1 componente / 0 huérfanos tanto en producto como en demo embed.html.||graph;buildGraph;orphans;connectivity;viewer|2026-07-31||3||0.78|1|2026-08-01T04:05:28.632Z
  c8d34189|decision|docs-benchmarks-tabbed|Docs home benchmarks consolidados en UNA sección tabbed (Benchmarks.astro, id="benchmarks") con 3 pestañas: Ranking (tabla Linear vs RRF nDCG/MRR paridad 0.776/0.917, 8 gold queries, npm run bench:rrf), Workflow (5 ahorros de sesión en tarjetas compactas), Formato (barras JSON vs TOON + 3 stats). Se eliminaron ImpactShowcase.astro y TokenSavings.astro (fusión en pestañas). Card RRF del WhatNew perdió los números. i18n: keys tokenSavings/impactSection reemplazadas por benchmarks.{tabs,ranking,workflow,format} en 8 locales. Commit 2e8be8e.||docs;benchmark;rrf;i18n|2026-07-31||1|v3-7-0-released|0.89|1|2026-08-01T04:07:24.176Z
  f035951e|knowledge|mcp-registry-cache-lag|The MCP Registry search endpoint `GET /v0/servers?search=toon-memory` (no version filter) serves a stale CDN-cached copy (showed 3.6.1 for ~5+ min after publish). To verify the live version, query `?version=latest` (or `?version=X.Y.Z`) — those returned 3.7.0 immediately. The publish API itself confirmed "✓ Server io.github.LuiggiVal08/toon-memory version 3.7.0".||mcp-registry;verification;release|2026-07-31||1||0.79|1|2026-08-01T03:59:22.587Z
  1b048e3e|knowledge|v3-7-0-released|v3.7.0 published: commit 81f3a3d on main, release/tag v3.7.0, npm `toon-memory@3.7.0` live, MCP Registry `io.github.LuiggiVal08/toon-memory` v3.7.0 = latest (description "40 tools"). Publish workflow (3 parallel jobs: build guard → npm + MCP Registry) all green, run 30656554816.||release;v3.7.0;npm;mcp-registry|2026-07-31||1|publish-workflow-parallel-jobs rrf-fusion-final-design|0.99|1|2026-08-01T03:59:22.587Z
  6fc78505|decision|publish-workflow-parallel-jobs|PUBLISH WORKFLOW (.github/workflows/publish.yml) refactorizado a 3 jobs: (1) `build` — checkout, npm ci, build, test, guard "package.json version == release tag" (cazaría el error del doble v3.6.0), npm pack, upload artifact `npm-package` (tgz); (2) `publish-npm` needs:build — setup-node con registry-url, download artifact, `npm publish --provenance --access public ./package/*.tgz` (publicar un tarball NO re-ejecuta prepublishOnly=build+test, verificado en docs npm: solo corre al publicar desde el directorio); (3) `publish-mcp-registry` needs:build — checkout, mcp-publisher login github-oidc (id-token:write), jq set version en server.json desde GITHUB_REF, publish. Ambos publish jobs son independientes entre sí (comparten solo el gate de build) — un fallo en uno no bloquea al otro. Publish del MCP registry: mcp-publisher solo sube server.json, no valida que el paquete npm exista → el orden npm→MCP no es requisito. Historial de fallos: v3.6.0 doble tag → npm 403 "cannot publish over previously published versions"; v3.6.0/v3.5.0 → MCP 422 "expected length <= 100" en server.json.description (arreglado acortando desc). server.json requiere descripcion <=100 chars. Usar npm ci (no npm install) para reproducibilidad.||ci;workflow;publish;npm;mcp-registry|2026-07-31||0|competitive-roadmap-2026-07|0.88|1|
  b31d9e30|decision|rrf-fusion-final-design|DISEÑO FINAL de RRF (benchmark scripts/bench-rrf.mjs decidió la variante). Fusion = rrfFuse([bm25Rank, bm25Rank, bm25Rank, centRank], rrfK(n)) con rrfK(n)=clamp[3,60] de round(sqrt(n)). IMPORTANCE se EXCLUYÓ de la fusión: en grafos pequeños su rank está dominado por ruido de recencia y arrastra el nDCG (variantes probadas: bbci=0.725, bbccci=0.648, bbbci=0.775, bbbc=0.776 PARITY). Resultado con 8 queries gold-fair: RRF nDCG 0.776 = linear 0.776, MRR 0.917 = 0.917 (1 win/1 loss/6 ties). El seedRank/exact-match ranker también se eliminó (stopwords lo volvían ruidoso). Se replicó por igual en src/lib/graph.ts (graphRecallDetailed) y src/lib/quality.ts (generateSmartRecall). k=60 textbook aplana ranks en grafos pequeños → adaptive k=√N. package.json ahora tiene "bench:rrf": "node scripts/bench-rrf.mjs".|scripts/bench-rrf.mjs:1|rrf;benchmark;graph;retrieval|2026-07-31||1|competitive-roadmap-2026-07|0.88|1|2026-08-01T04:07:24.176Z
  b80a2f39|decision|competitive-roadmap-2026-07|Competitive roadmap approved (Jul 2026). ADOPTED (all 6): (1) typed edges in links (type:key, backward-compatible), (2) RRF fusion flag in recall, (3) deterministic memory_reflect (tag co-occurrence, contradictions, hubs), (4) memory_supersede + as_of, (5) MCP tool annotations (readOnlyHint/destructiveHint) on all tools, (6) heuristic auto-promote from capture log (drafts, confidence ≤0.65, opt-in). PLUS: publish a real retrieval benchmark (LongMemEval-style on our own data) to close the only numeric gap vs MemPalace/Hindsight/Zep. DEFERRED (maybe later, re-evaluate): local Markdown/notes importer (idea #6 from Basic Memory two-way) — user not attracted to it now; revisit in future sessions.||roadmap;competitive;decision;philosophy|2026-07-31||6|competitive-analysis-2026-07|0.89|1|2026-08-01T04:07:24.176Z
  be6a887c|knowledge|competitive-analysis-2026-07|Competitive analysis vs Mem0, Supermemory, Basic Memory, MemPalace, Hindsight, Zep (Jul 2026). Our edges: TOON -22.5% tokens, zero runtime deps, no LLM/cloud, deterministic, 15-agent hooks, quality+confidence, TTL, pin, sessions, context_* tools, budget recall. Their edges: semantic/LLM retrieval accuracy (MemPalace 96.6% R@5 LongMemEval), auto-ingestion of conversations, two-way human-readable Markdown (Basic Memory), typed graph relations (Basic Memory/MemPalace), fact invalidation + temporal queries (Zep/MemPalace), reflect/synthesis (Hindsight), MCP tool annotations (Basic Memory), RRF+rerank (Hindsight). Adoptable without breaking philosophy: typed edges in links (type:key), RRF fusion flag in recall, deterministic memory_reflect, memory_supersede + as_of, MCP annotations on 37 tools, local markdown/notes importer (one-way), heuristic auto-promote from capture log (drafts, low confidence). Deliberately NOT copying: cloud/LLM extraction, remote embeddings (violates zero-deps). Gap: we have no public retrieval benchmark.||competitive;analysis;roadmap;philosophy|2026-07-31||4|bm25-vs-embeddings-decision no-cloud-decision zero-deps-philosophy|0.99|1|2026-08-01T04:07:24.176Z
  51868a40|knowledge|release-roadmap-post-engram|Post-implementation roadmap for engram features:\n1. Update README.md with new features (path_scope, budget, origin, soft-delete, resolve/suppress tools)\n2. Update docs/ (Astro site) — tool docs, TOON format changes, new params\n3. Update compromised sections of home page in all languages (en, es, etc.)\n4. Update manifests (package.json version, etc.)\n5. Atomic commits per convention (feat:, fix:, docs:, etc.)\n6. Push changes to remote\n7. Create new git tag with bumped version\n8. Create new GitHub release||release;roadmap;engram;changelog|2026-07-30||0||0.79|1
  bd8243e9|pattern|new-tools-usage|New tools added: memory_resolve (restore soft-deleted entries), memory_suppress (mark obsolete). memory_forget now soft-deletes by default; use hard:true for permanent deletion.||tools;soft-delete;usage|2026-07-30||3||0.80|1|2026-07-31T11:58:32.180Z
  ee732474|knowledge|engram-features-implemented|Implemented 6 features inspired by Engram into toon-memory:\n1. **Path Scoping** (graph.ts: `path_scope` field 14): Entries can be scoped to file paths via glob patterns. `memory_remember` accepts `path_scope`. `memory_recall`/`memory_search` filter by `path_scope`. Added `globMatch()` helper.\n\n2. **Budget Control** (graph.ts: renderCompact): Replaced simple `compact` boolean with `budget: "tiny"\|"normal"\|"deep"`. `tiny` = key+1 line (~50 tokens), `normal` = compact with tags/edges, `deep` = all fields. Backward compatible with `compact: true`.\n\n3. **Origin Separation** (graph.ts: `origin` field 15, quality.ts): Entries track `human\|agent\|inferred` origin. qualityScore gives +0.1 for human, -0.05 for inferred. `memory_stats` shows origin breakdown.\n\n4. **Proactive Recall** (opencode-plugin.ts): `tool.execute.after` enhanced to also recall by tool name keywords when no file path is found. Uses `budget: "tiny"` for token efficiency.\n\n5. **Soft-delete** (tools.ts memory_forget/memory_resolve/memory_suppress): `memory_forget` soft-deletes by default (sets `status=obsolete`). `memory_resolve` restores. `memory_suppress` marks obsolete. Added `hard: true` flag for permanent deletion. `graphRecallDetailed` filters obsolete entries.\n\n6. **Enhanced Lint** (context.ts health): Missing-evidence check (path_scope without file). Stale-claims check (overlapping content in same category). Origin breakdown in overview. Status tracking in stats.|src/lib/graph.ts:21, src/mcp/tools.ts:26, src/lib/quality.ts:29, src/lib/context.ts:482, src/cli/opencode-plugin.ts:62|engram;path-scope;budget;proactive-recall;soft-delete;lint|2026-07-30||0||0.79|1
  0665af4d|architecture|mcp-apps-extensions-init-handler|Added MCP Apps protocol support by overriding the initialize handler in server.ts:\n1. Set `capabilities.experimental` with `io.modelcontextprotocol/ui: {}` in McpServer constructor options\n2. Override `server.server.setRequestHandler(InitializeRequestSchema, ...)` to include `extensions: { "io.modelcontextprotocol/ui": {} }` in InitializeResult\n3. Migrated from `@modelcontextprotocol/server` to `@modelcontextprotocol/sdk` (same API, official package)\n4. The SDK still only supports protocol version 2025-11-25, but the extensions field is added to the response for MCP Apps negotiation|src/mcp/server.ts:15-30|mcp-apps;extensions;initialize;protocol|2026-07-30||0|viewer-mcp-apps-integration session-store-details esbuild-vs-tsc-decision|0.98|1
  8a7e25e7|decision|viewer-mcp-apps-integration|MCP Apps integration for the viewer: registered `ui://viewer` resource that generates the D3.js force-directed graph HTML with live data, and `memory_visualize` tool with `_meta.ui.resourceUri` pointing to it. The tool accepts an optional `query` parameter. `buildViewerData()` now returns empty data instead of `process.exit(0)` for empty memory. Resource is served dynamically — each request builds fresh data. Viewer reload button uses `location.reload()` which re-fetches the `ui://` resource in MCP Apps hosts. Total tools: 30, total resources: 4.|src/mcp/resources.ts|viewer;mcp-apps;ui;decision|2026-07-29||0|viewer-html-generation viewer-data-flow resources-registration|0.98|1|
  e4b00a8c|knowledge|viewer-live-observations-bridge|Live mode watchea todo MEMORY_DIR (data.toon + observations.toon). Observations registran cada tool call del agente (recall, remember, stats, etc.). Al cambiar observations.toon, el server re-construye ViewerData y envía SSE aunque data.toon no haya cambiado. El badge LIVE parpadea en verde para mostrar actividad.|src/viewer/server.ts|viewer;live;sse;observations;bridge|2026-07-29||1|viewer-serve-mode viewer-static-snapshot observations-module viewer-serve-mode session-auto-promotion-details viewer-html-generation|1.00|1|2026-07-29T17:18:16.367Z
  b2c3c0e1|pattern|viewer-sidebar-graph-sync|Pattern: viewer connector between sidebar entry list and graph uses the selectEntry() function which sets selectedEntry global, re-renders entry list (adds .selected class), shows detail panel via showDetail(), highlights the node in the graph via graph.highlightNode(), switches to the Detail tab. Clicking on a graph node does the same via the node click handler.|src/viewer/html.ts|pattern;viewer;selection;sync;sidebar-graph|2026-07-29||10|sidebar-entry-list-pattern viewer-data-flow viewer-css-variable-pattern|1.00|1|2026-08-01T03:59:14.993Z
  a4b1a64f|architecture|viewer-data-flow|Architecture: viewer data flow starts in buildViewerData() which reads .toon memory, parses entries, builds the graph, and returns structured ViewerData (nodes, edges, categories, tagCounts, totalEntries). The data is serialized to JSON and injected into the HTML template. On the client side, DATA is parsed once and used by all panels: graph (D3 force layout), stats (category/tag charts), timeline (date groups), detail (entry metadata).|src/viewer/data.ts|architecture;viewer;data-flow;json;serialization|2026-07-29||7|viewer-html-generation viewer-tabs-system cli-setup-routing|1.00|1|2026-07-31T20:46:46.935Z
  b0251ac4|decision|viewer-tooltip-design|Decision: viewer uses pointer-events:none on tooltips to prevent them from intercepting mouse events. The tooltip is a fixed-position div that follows the cursor via mousemove listener. Position calculation flips the tooltip to the left if it would overflow the viewport. This approach is simpler than a CSS-only tooltip and allows rich HTML content (colored spans, tag chips).|src/viewer/html.ts|decision;viewer;tooltip;ux;interaction|2026-07-29||3|sidebar-resizer-layout-bug viewer-css-variable-pattern viewer-theme-toggle|1.00|1|2026-07-31T20:46:46.935Z
  aa943197|pattern|viewer-css-variable-pattern|Pattern: viewer uses CSS custom properties (--sidebar-w, --bg, --text, --brand, etc.) for all dynamic styling. This enables theme switching via .light class toggling CSS variable values, sidebar resize by updating --sidebar-w, consistent color usage across all components. The approach avoids JS-driven style changes and keeps all visual logic in CSS.|src/viewer/html.ts|pattern;viewer;css-variables;theming;design|2026-07-29||3|viewer-theme-toggle-pattern sidebar-resizer-layout-bug viewer-theme-toggle|1.00|1|2026-07-29T13:08:53.050Z
  2d0a984e|architecture|viewer-node-edge-sizing|Architecture: viewer node sizing uses a formula based on accessCount: radius = 4 + min(accessCount * 0.8, 8). This means nodes range from 4px (never accessed) to 12px (max). Edge thickness also varies: width = 0.5 + min(shared connections * 0.3, 3), where shared connections is the smaller of the two nodes' connection counts. Both formulas cap growth to prevent visual distortion.|src/viewer/html.ts|architecture;viewer;sizing;radius;visualization|2026-07-29||1|graph-edge-thickness graph-node-radius graph-bfs-traversal|1.00|1|2026-07-29T13:07:40.627Z
  5e8f5823|knowledge|viewer-zoom-controls|Knowledge: viewer zoom controls implement D3 zoom behavior with scaleExtent [0.1, 4]. Three buttons: zoom in (1.5x), zoom out (0.67x), reset (identity). The zoom is applied to a g wrapper element, not the SVG itself, so UI overlay elements (controls, legend, minimap) stay fixed. reset uses d3.zoomIdentity for a clean transition back to the initial state.|src/viewer/html.ts|knowledge;viewer;zoom;controls;d3|2026-07-29||2|d3-graph-viewer viewer-physics-controls viewer-force-graph|1.00|1|2026-07-29T13:08:53.050Z
  a1b11344|architecture|viewer-highlight-system|Architecture: viewer node highlight system provides 3 interaction modes: node hover (mouseover shows tooltip + highlights neighbors), node click (selects entry + switches to detail tab), and search/filter mode (matches by id/content/tags + category filter). Highlight types: hover highlights neighbors with increased radius + opacity fade for non-neighbors, selected gets glow + brand stroke, search dims non-matches to 0.08 opacity.|src/viewer/html.ts|architecture;viewer;highlight;selection;search|2026-07-29||1|graph-node-radius graph-glow-effect sidebar-entry-list-pattern|1.00|1|2026-07-29T13:07:40.627Z
  a0f3fe61|architecture|viewer-detail-panel|Architecture: viewer detail panel shows full entry metadata: category badge (colored), key/title, content (monospace block), file link (if any), date, quality score (brand colored, bold), access count, TTL (if set), last accessed date, tags as chips, and linked entries as clickable pills. Clicking a linked entry navigates to that entry via selectEntryById() which is exposed as a global function.|src/viewer/html.ts|architecture;viewer;detail;metadata;links|2026-07-29||1|toon-file-format-details viewer-timeline-panel sidebar-entry-list-pattern|1.00|1|2026-07-29T13:08:14.062Z
  a4677a7e|architecture|viewer-timeline-panel|Architecture: viewer timeline panel groups entries by date in reverse chronological order. Each timeline entry shows date, category badge (colored left border), key, and content preview (100 chars). Clicking navigates to the entry's detail. A vertical line (timeline-line) connects entries visually. Entries without dates are grouped under 'unknown'. Timeline-header shows total count.|src/viewer/html.ts|architecture;viewer;timeline;chronological|2026-07-29||2|sidebar-entry-list-pattern viewer-stats-panel toon-file-format-details|1.00|1|2026-07-31T20:46:46.935Z
  ccc756ea|architecture|viewer-stats-panel|Architecture: viewer topic rendering - the stats panel shows bar charts for category distribution and a tag cloud for top 20 tags. Category bars use the COLORS map for fill colors and animate width via CSS transition (0.6s cubic-bezier). Tag cloud pills show count in parentheses. Stats also show total entries, edge count, average quality, and max access count in big stat cards.|src/viewer/html.ts|architecture;viewer;stats;charts;visualization|2026-07-29||1|viewer-html-generation sidebar-entry-list-pattern cli-setup-routing|1.00|1|2026-07-29T13:08:14.062Z
  9680002b|decision|viewer-physics-controls|Decision: viewer physics sliders use HTML range inputs with live updates. Three controls: Charge (-300 to 0, default -120), Link Distance (20 to 200, default 70), Center Strength (0 to 1, default 0.05). Changes update the simulation forces and restart with alpha 0.5. Panel toggled via button. This lets users fine-tune the layout without needing to understand D3 force parameters.|src/viewer/html.ts|decision;viewer;physics;ux;interaction|2026-07-29||6|graph-physics-controls viewer-force-graph graph-force-layout|1.00|1|2026-07-29T13:27:24.420Z
  08e022b3|knowledge|viewer-tabs-system|Knowledge: viewer tabs system - 4 tabs (Graph, Stats, Timeline, Detail). Tabs use data-tab attributes to match with panel IDs (#panel-graph, #panel-stats, etc.). Only the active tab-panel is visible (display:block). Switching tabs triggers graph.resize() if switching to the graph tab (to recalculate layout after the panel becomes visible and has dimensions). switchTab() helper function handles tab switching.|src/viewer/html.ts|knowledge;viewer;tabs;panel;navigation|2026-07-29||5|viewer-keyboard-shortcuts viewer-html-generation viewer-standalone|1.00|1|2026-07-29T13:10:26.720Z
  9206d469|pattern|viewer-theme-toggle-pattern|Pattern: theme toggle stores preference in localStorage (key: 'toon-viewer-theme'). Dark theme uses dark background with brand purple. Light theme swaps to light background. Toggle button cycles icons. CSS variables handle all color references, so a single .light class toggle updates the entire page. Tooltips get adjusted backdrop-filter in light mode.|src/viewer/html.ts|pattern;viewer;theme;dark;light;localstorage|2026-07-29||1|viewer-theme-toggle d3-graph-viewer viewer-standalone|1.00|1|2026-07-29T13:08:53.050Z
  661f1419|pattern|sidebar-entry-list-pattern|Pattern: entry viewer sidebar renders the entry list with filtering and search. Filter buttons for each category (decision/bug/pattern/knowledge/architecture) plus 'All'. Search input filters by id, content, or tags. Entries show category badge, key, content preview (2 lines), and tag chips. Clicking selects the entry and switches to Detail tab. Selected entries get .selected class with brand border.|src/viewer/html.ts|pattern;viewer;sidebar;filter;search|2026-07-29||8|toon-file-format-details entry-linking-patterns shared-tag-auto-linking|1.00|1|2026-07-29T17:18:16.367Z
  c814e3b0|architecture|skills-architecture|Architecture: the skills directory contains skill definitions for agent workflows. skills/toon-memory.md is the main skill that teaches agents how to use toon-memory effectively. Skills are loaded by the agent via the skill tool when a task matches the skill description. Each skill has a name, description (used for matching), and location (path to SKILL.md with instructions).|skills/|architecture;skills;workflows;agents|2026-07-28||0|observations-module lock-file-mechanism config-writer-architecture|0.98|1|
  1ddef22a|architecture|codebase-memory-mcp-integration|Architecture: codebase-memory-mcp integration via auto-loaded rules file auto-loads the codebase knowledge graph for structural code queries. It augments traditional grep/glob with graph-based search (search_graph, trace_path, get_code_snippet, query_graph). The codebase graph indexes LSP call/usage resolution and provides cross-referencing. Used together with toon-memory for comprehensive context.|src/cli/agents.ts|architecture;codebase;graph;mcp;opencode|2026-07-29||3|esbuild-build-pipeline consolidation-module session-auto-promotion-details|1.00|1|2026-07-31T11:58:32.180Z
  d6ae9c31|architecture|scoring-access-tracking|Architecture: scoring module in src/mcp/scoring.ts provides entry relevance scoring. findRelatedEntries() finds entries related to a given query by checking tags, content overlap, and links. bumpAccessed() increments the accessCount and updates lastAccessed timestamp when an entry is recalled. Access tracking is persisted to the .toon file on every recall. Used by memory_recall and memory_smart_recall.|src/mcp/scoring.ts|architecture;scoring;relevance;access-tracking|2026-07-28||1|drift-detection git-integration quality-access-tracking|0.99|1|2026-07-30T16:13:07.557Z
  495dff45|architecture|session-store-details|Architecture: session store in src/mcp/session-store.ts manages agent session lifecycle. createSession() records a new session with branch, start time, and empty file list. touchSession() updates the last-seen timestamp. addSessionFile() records files touched during the session. getSessions() lists active sessions. Supports conflict detection by comparing file sets between sessions on different branches.|src/mcp/session-store.ts|architecture;session;store;lifecycle|2026-07-28||2|session-start-hook session-pruning-pattern session-store-architecture|0.99|1|2026-07-30T16:13:07.203Z
  cb3bb48d|architecture|consolidation-module|Architecture: consolidation module in src/mcp/consolidation.ts provides content deduplication. consolidateEntries() removes entries with identical content (keeps the one with the highest quality score). mergeSimilar() uses Jaccard similarity > 0.5 to find near-duplicates and merge them. Both operations create backups before modifying data. Used by memory_consolidate and memory_merge_similar tools.|src/mcp/consolidation.ts|architecture;consolidation;dedup;merge|2026-07-28||4|near-duplicate-detection consolidation-algorithm archive-module|0.99|1|2026-07-31T11:58:32.180Z
  8fd022fa|architecture|observations-module|Architecture: observations module in src/mcp/observations.ts manages the observation log. readObservations() reads observations.toon, writeObservation() appends a new observation. Each observation has: tool (name of tool that was called), file (file being operated on), timestamp (ISO date). The module also handles auto-pruning at 500 entries. Observations are stored in the same TOON format as memory entries.|src/mcp/observations.ts|architecture;observations;log;capture|2026-07-28||3|observation-auto-prune capture-hook-architecture session-auto-promotion-details|0.99|1|2026-07-29T13:27:24.420Z
  3451e598|architecture|entry-id-generation|Architecture: entry IDs use format 'XXXXXXXX' (8 hex chars) generated from timestamp + random. generateId() takes the current Unix timestamp in ms, converts to hex (last 6 chars), and appends 2 random hex chars. This gives ~65K unique IDs per millisecond without collisions. IDs are short (8 chars) for token efficiency but not meant to be human-readable.|src/mcp/entries.ts|architecture;id;generation;hex;unique|2026-07-28||0|entries-module toon-format-decision lock-file-mechanism|0.99|1|
  cf3fb2fc|architecture|lock-file-mechanism|Architecture: lock file (.toon-memory/memory/.lock) uses a format with PID@hostname and timestamp. acquireLock() writes this file using writeFileSync (atomic on most OS for small files). If the file exists and is older than 5 seconds, it's considered stale and overwritten (deadlock recovery). Locks are released explicitly by releaseLock() or cleaned up on process exit.|src/lib/lock.ts|architecture;lock;concurrency;atomic;deadlock|2026-07-28||0|file-locking-pattern drift-detection session-pruning-pattern|0.99|1|
  5ba22d13|knowledge|i18n-and-localization|Knowledge: i18n is handled through 8 translated README files (README.es.md, README.de.md, README.fr.md, README.ja.md, README.ko.md, README.pt-br.md, README.zh.md). The docs site has its own i18n via Astro's built-in i18n support. CLI messages and tool descriptions are in English only. The AGENTS.md allows the agent to respond in the user's language (Spanish in this case).|README.es.md|knowledge;i18n;languages;readme;docs|2026-07-28||1|docs-site-architecture mcp-tool-error-handling memory-io-layer|0.99|1|2026-07-29T13:06:36.814Z
  cc61641b|knowledge|project-constants|Knowledge: project constants in src/cli/constants.ts defines projectRoot (resolved from package.json location or CWD), editorConfig paths, and version string. Used by all modules that need filesystem paths. The projectRoot discovery walks up directories looking for package.json or .toon-memory directory. Falls back to process.cwd().|src/cli/constants.ts|knowledge;constants;paths;project-root|2026-07-28||1|memory-io-layer context-generation-tools backup-rotation-pattern|0.99|1|2026-07-29T17:18:16.367Z
  6ce8045d|knowledge|capture-hooks-per-agent|Knowledge: capture hooks are stored per-agent-framework in each agent's config directory. OpenCode uses .opencode/rules/, Claude Code uses CLAUDE.md, Cursor uses .cursorrules, Continue uses .continuerc, Gemini uses .gemini/config/*.md. Each config installs the capture binary (dist/cli/capture.js) as a tool_use hook. The binary writes observations to observations.toon when a tool is invoked.|src/cli/config-writer.ts|knowledge;capture;hooks;agents;config|2026-07-28||0|agent-framework-integration agents-module config-writer-architecture|0.98|1|
  10b9dce3|knowledge|viewer-static-snapshot|Knowledge: the viewer receives data as an injected JSON blob (const DATA = ${jsonData}) at HTML generation time. It does NOT fetch from any API or read the .toon file. This means the viewer is a static HTML snapshot, not a live view, it works offline with no server, to refresh you regenerate. The --serve flag wraps the same HTML in a basic HTTP server. --live flag adds SSE for auto-refresh.|src/viewer/html.ts|knowledge;viewer;static;offline;architecture|2026-07-29||4|viewer-html-generation no-cloud-decision prompts-ts-error|1.00|1|2026-07-31T11:58:32.180Z
  824b0ac9|knowledge|drift-detection|Knowledge: drift detection compares lastAccessed date against git file modification times. If a memory entry references a file and that file has been modified more recently than the entry was accessed, the entry is flagged as potentially stale. Quality score is reduced by up to 0.15 for drifted entries. Detected during smart_recall and context generation.|src/lib/quality.ts|knowledge;drift;stale;quality;git|2026-07-28||3|git-integration toon-file-format-details toon-format-decision|0.99|1|2026-07-29T13:13:30.218Z
  7c96a6c2|knowledge|session-auto-promotion-details|Knowledge: session promotion automatically promotes observations accessed 3+ times in a session to permanent memory entries. Tracked via session access map. Happens on session end or periodically. Prevents loss of frequently-used transient knowledge. The promotion uses memory_remember with the observation content, auto-assigning a key from the tool name and file path.|src/mcp/session-store.ts|knowledge;session;promotion;auto;transient|2026-07-28||1|session-auto-promotion file-locking-pattern opencode-plugin-auto-loading|0.99|1|2026-07-30T16:13:07.203Z
  1520ef6b|knowledge|context-generation-tools|Knowledge: context generation in src/lib/context.ts produces structured output for context_* tools. context_brief returns relevant memory + active sessions + project health. context_generate returns full system prompt with project info (from package.json), git state (branch, recent commits), relevant memory entries, and active sessions. context_focus returns hyper-focused data for a specific symbol/task including related files and tests.|src/lib/context.ts|knowledge;context;generation;structured|2026-07-28||4|token-efficient-context context-brief-architecture benchmark-scripts|0.98|1|2026-07-29T17:18:16.367Z
  75494219|knowledge|git-integration|Knowledge: git integration in src/lib/git.ts provides fileMtimes() to check when files were last modified via git. Used for drift detection in quality scoring. If a file has been modified by the user but the memory entry hasn't been updated, quality decreases. Also checks git log for recency signals. Integration uses execSync to run git commands.|src/lib/git.ts|knowledge;git;drift;quality;mtime|2026-07-28||0|session-start-hook no-cloud-decision jsonl-format|0.98|1|
  76ac11a7|pattern|deterministic-graph-algorithms|Pattern: all graph algorithms (centrality, BM25, BFS) are deterministic with no randomness. Centrality uses degree centrality (number of connections). BM25 uses fixed k1=1.5, b=0.75. Sort for tiebreaking uses consistent key ordering. This ensures the same query always returns the same results, critical for reproducible agent behavior.|src/lib/graph.ts|pattern;graph;deterministic;reproducibility|2026-07-28||0|graph-bfs-traversal shared-tag-auto-linking mcp-tool-error-handling|0.99|1|
  962a42b1|pattern|graph-bfs-traversal|Pattern: graph traversal uses BFS for shortest path (memory_graph_path) and neighbor expansion (graph recall mode). Shortest path uses a standard queue-based BFS with visited set, returning the path as array of entry keys. Graph recall does 1-hop or 2-hop expansion from seed nodes, returning the subgraph with edges. Both are O(V+E) on the memory graph.|src/lib/graph.ts|pattern;graph;bfs;shortest-path;traversal|2026-07-28||0|graph-recall-algorithm graph-centrality-algorithm entry-linking-patterns|0.98|1|
  9db55138|pattern|entry-linking-patterns|Pattern: entries also link via explicit links field and [[wiki refs]] in content. parseEntries() extracts both. Explicit links are stored as array in the entry. Wiki refs are parsed from content using regex /\[\[([^\]]+)\]\]/g. All link types (explicit, wiki, shared-tag) are merged into the graph adjacency list for unified traversal.|src/lib/graph.ts|pattern;graph;links;wiki;parsing|2026-07-28||1|shared-tag-auto-linking graph-edge-types utils-module|0.99|1|2026-07-31T21:11:49.729Z
  1b8010ac|pattern|shared-tag-auto-linking|Pattern: entries auto-link when they share 2+ tags. buildGraph() in graph.ts iterates all entry pairs and adds an edge if they share >= 2 tags. Skip optimization: entries with 0-1 tags are skipped from the outer loop since they cannot match the threshold. This O(n²) algorithm runs on every build but is fast enough for <500 entries.|src/lib/graph.ts|pattern;graph;edges;tags;auto-link|2026-07-28||3|near-duplicate-detection entries-module benchmark-graph-mismatch|0.99|1|2026-07-31T21:11:49.729Z
  429b6ffb|bug|viewer-css-duplicates|Bug: viewer CSS had a duplicate .timeline-entry rule and a duplicate .graph-container svg rule. The grid background pseudoelement was rendered below the SVG due to z-index stacking. These were cosmetic but caused redundant CSS.|src/viewer/html.ts|bug;viewer;css;duplicate;cosmetic|2026-07-29||2|sidebar-resizer-layout-bug d3js-viewer-decision viewer-serve-exit-bug|1.00|1|2026-07-29T13:09:29.356Z
  b6189a1d|bug|prompts-ts-error|Bug: TS error in prompts.ts - a pre-existing type error unrelated to the viewer/system changes. Error was already present before any edits. Does not block build (esbuild doesn't type-check) but fails npx tsc --noEmit. Needs separate fix: type annotation mismatch in the prompts definitions.|src/mcp/prompts.ts|bug;typescript;type-error;preexisting|2026-07-28||0|esbuild-vs-tsc-decision mcp-tool-error-handling build-order-race|0.99|1|
  7f6aab93|bug|build-order-race|Bug: Build had implicit dependency order (bin -> mcp -> cli) but the build script used Promise.all originally, causing race conditions where mcp/server.js was referenced before being built. Fix: changed to sequential && chaining to guarantee build order. Also discovered that src/mcp/server.ts imports from lib/ which must be resolved before bundling.|package.json|bug;build;race;order;sequential|2026-07-28||1|benchmark-graph-mismatch viewer-serve-exit-bug npm-dependencies|0.99|1|2026-07-29T13:13:16.060Z
  c4e19039|bug|benchmark-graph-mismatch|Bug: Benchmark script (bench-viewer.mjs) produced graph stats (167 edges) that didn't match the real buildGraph in graph.ts (171 edges). Cause: benchmark used a simpler edge-building algorithm that didn't include shared-tag edges (2+ shared tags). Fix: rewrote benchmark to use the same buildGraph logic, now produces matching 171 edges.|scripts/bench-viewer.mjs|bug;benchmark;graph;edges;mismatch|2026-07-28||3|benchmark-scripts bm25-vs-embeddings-decision docs-site-architecture|0.99|1|2026-07-31T21:11:49.729Z
  dbbb5f41|bug|sidebar-resizer-layout-bug|Bug: sidebar resizer was a grid item in a grid-template-columns layout, causing layout shifts when the sidebar width changed via CSS variable. Fix: changed resizer to position: absolute with left: var(--sidebar-w), and .main to position: relative. This decoupled the resizer from the grid layout and allowed smooth sidebar resize without grid recalculation.|src/viewer/html.ts|bug;viewer;layout;resizer;css|2026-07-29||3|viewer-theme-toggle viewer-standalone viewer-serve-exit-bug|1.00|1|2026-07-29T13:13:16.060Z
  84b4d218|bug|viewer-serve-exit-bug|Bug: viewer --serve called process.exit(0) after viewerServe() but before the HTTP server could bind. The exit(0) was in the non-serve code path but ran unconditionally due to fallthrough in the if/else chain. Fix: moved process.exit(0) inside the non-serve callback and restructured as if/else if/else to prevent fallthrough to 'Unknown command'.|src/cli/setup.ts|bug;viewer;server;exit;race-condition|2026-07-28||0|stdio-vs-sse-decision cli-setup-routing toon-format-decision|0.97|1|
  67aaedf7|decision|auto-merge-on-duplicate|Decision: memory_remember auto-merges on duplicate key (same key = update, not error). This simplifies agent usage - agents can update entries without checking existence first. Auto-merge strategy: union of tags, max of confidence/quality scores, merge links, update date to latest. Verbatim mode (skip auto-tagging) available for precision. No cascading merge on linked entries.|src/mcp/tools.ts|decision;merge;dedup;upsert;ergonomics|2026-07-28||1|entries-module no-cloud-decision jaccard-merge|0.99|1|2026-07-29T13:05:42.677Z
  18c6638c|decision|no-cloud-decision|Decision: no central storage or cloud sync - memory stays local to each project. Rationale: security (no data leaves the machine), simplicity (no auth, no API keys, no servers), speed (no network latency), offline-first (works without internet). Users who want cloud sync can use GitHub Gist export/import or check .toon files into git. This is a feature, not a limitation.|README.md|decision;privacy;offline;local;security|2026-07-28||1|export-gist-format memory-io-layer esbuild-vs-tsc-decision|0.99|1|2026-07-31T11:58:26.709Z
  5fd99199|decision|quality-scoring-decision|Decision: access counting with staleness decay for quality scoring rather than LLM-based quality assessment. Access count + recency approximates usefulness without LLM calls. Entries accessed recently score higher. Staleness decay (-0.2 after 30 days) removes stale knowledge. Combined with content-based signals (tags, links, specificity) for a robust 0-1 score. Deterministic, predictable, explainable.|src/lib/quality.ts|decision;quality;scoring;staleness;deterministic|2026-07-28||2|quality-scoring-pattern quality-score-formula quality-access-tracking|0.99|1|2026-07-31T11:58:26.709Z
  ac8ec59f|decision|bm25-vs-embeddings-decision|Decision to use BM25 over embedding models for search: BM25 is deterministic, requires no LLM, no model downloads, no GPU. Works offline. Perfect for code search where exact term matching matters. Trade-off: misses semantic similarity that embeddings capture. Mitigation: synonym expansion and fuzzy matching add coverage. For a dev tool, BM25's precision on code terms is more valuable than semantic fuzziness.|src/lib/graph.ts|decision;search;bm25;embeddings;offline|2026-07-28||2|stdio-vs-sse-decision esbuild-vs-tsc-decision fuzzy-search-module|0.99|1|2026-08-01T03:59:14.993Z
  120fbaa7|decision|d3js-viewer-decision|Decision: D3.js v7 via CDN for the viewer instead of bundling a graph library. Rationale: D3 is the de facto standard for force-directed graphs, CDN avoids adding 250KB+ to the bundle, the viewer HTML is self-contained anyway. Canvas was considered for rendering but SVG was chosen for simplicity, accessibility, and export support. Cytoscape.js was rejected due to heavier API and licensing.|src/viewer/html.ts|decision;viewer;d3js;cdn;visualization|2026-07-29||6|viewer-html-generation viewer-standalone d3-graph-viewer|1.00|1|2026-07-31T20:46:46.935Z
  fdb6843f|decision|esbuild-vs-tsc-decision|Decision to use esbuild over tsc for build: esbuild is 10-100x faster than tsc, produces bundled output (single JS file for MCP server), supports --define for version injection. tsc is used only for type checking (npx tsc --noEmit in CI). The trade-off: no type checking during build means type errors slip through if not caught separately. CI catches them.|package.json|decision;build;esbuild;tsc;speed|2026-07-28||3|ci-workflow-config stdio-vs-sse-decision typescript-configuration|0.98|1|2026-07-30T05:01:48.315Z
  d2669967|decision|stdio-vs-sse-decision|Decision to use StdioServerTransport (stdio MCP) over SSE (HTTP MCP): Stdio is simpler, requires no HTTP server, no port assignment, no CORS. Ideal for local CLI-based AI agents (OpenCode, Claude, Cursor). SSE adds complexity for zero benefit in local scenarios. The trade-off: only one client at a time, but memory uses file locking for concurrent safety anyway.|src/mcp/server.ts|decision;mcp;transport;stdio;sse|2026-07-28||3|viewer-standalone jsonl-format utils-module|0.99|1|2026-07-31T01:52:40.128Z
  03c1fc4d|decision|toon-format-decision|Decision to use TOON format over JSON/Markdown: TOON is compact (~250 bytes/entry vs ~500+ for JSON), pipe-delimited (human-readable, grep-friendly), version-controllable (diff-friendly). Preserves field order for deterministic diffs. JSONL was considered but TOON offers better density. Markdown was rejected because structured data needs parsing. The @toon-format/toon library handles serialization.|src/mcp/memory-io.ts|decision;format;toon;json;markdown;storage|2026-07-28||5|toon-file-format-details memory-io-layer jsonl-format|0.99|1|2026-07-31T01:52:40.128Z
  578c2abd|knowledge|toon-file-format-details|TOON file format: custom pipe-delimited compact format via @toon-format/toon. Header with version, separator config. Each entry has fields: key, category, content, tags, date, accessed, file, ttl, lastAccessed, links. Compact storage (~250 bytes per entry). Human-readable and version-controllable. Archive.toon uses same format for old entries.|src/mcp/memory-io.ts|separated), date, accessed, file, ttl, lastAccessed. Compact storage (~250 bytes per entry). Human-readable and version-controllable. Archive.toon uses same format for old entries.;format;toon;storage;compact|src/mcp/memory-io.ts|toon;format;storage;compact;human-readable|2026|toon-format-decision memory-io-layer jsonl-format|1.00|0|0.99
  91203b13|knowledge|agent-framework-integration|Agent frameworks integration: 15+ agents supported via auto-detection in agents.ts and config-writer.ts. Each agent gets capture hooks + memory_recall auto-loading. File watcher (watchMemory via fs.watch) reloads memory on changes. OpenCode gets the most advanced integration (beacon event, tool.execute.after hook). Claude Code via CLAUDE.md. Others via .cursorrules, .continuerc, .gemini/config, etc.|src/cli/agents.ts|agents;integration;frameworks;auto-detection|2026-07-28||2|agents-module config-writer-architecture capture-hook-architecture|0.99|1|2026-07-31T11:58:32.180Z
  54f02734|knowledge|benchmark-scripts|Benchmark scripts in scripts/: benchmark-toon.mjs (TOON format read/write perf), benchmark-impact.mjs (impact analysis), bench-context-tools.mjs (context generation perf), bench-full-impact.mjs (full impact analysis), bench-compress-all.mjs (compression perf), bench-primer.mjs (system primer generation). bench-viewer.mjs produces graph stats (density, avg degree) to match buildGraph output.|scripts/|benchmark;scripts;performance;metrics|2026-07-28||3|docs-site-architecture npm-dependencies mcp-tool-history|0.99|1|2026-07-31T17:13:02.097Z
  c4308171|knowledge|installer-scripts|Installer scripts: install.sh (bash, Unix) and install.ps1 (PowerShell, Windows). Detects platform and installs to local bin or global. install.sh uses curl/wget to fetch the latest release tarball. install.ps1 uses Invoke-WebRequest. Both check for Node.js >= 18. Also installs shell completions (bash/zsh) and man pages. Uninstall via uninstall.sh or manual removal.|install.sh|installer;setup;cross-platform;node|2026-07-28||0|cli-setup-routing docs-site-architecture commands-module|0.98|1|
  b8b00fc2|knowledge|docs-site-architecture|Documentation is a separate Astro site in docs/ directory. Uses Astro for SSG, deployed via GitHub Pages. Supports 8 languages (en, es, zh, ja, ko, pt-br, de, fr) via Astro i18n. Features: 29 MCP tools cards with SVG icons, token system architecture diagrams, benchmark showcase with charts, sticky header, accessibility, SEO, professional design. Dev server via docs own scripts.|docs/|docs;astro;i18n;ssg;landing-page|2026-07-28||1|docs-i18n-keys viewer-html-generation mcp-tool-error-handling|0.99|1|2026-07-31T18:17:07.955Z
  d16aa3f9|knowledge|ci-workflow-config|CI configuration in .github/workflows/ci.yml: Triggers on push/PR to main. Matrix strategy: Node 20 and 22. Steps: checkout, setup-node (matrix version), npm ci, npm run build, npm test. Also runs npx tsc --noEmit for type checking (no ESLint configured). Separate workflows: docs.yml (docs site deploy) and publish.yml (npm publish on release tag).|.github/workflows/ci.yml|ci;github-actions;matrix;node|2026-07-28||1|typescript-configuration vitest-test-infrastructure esbuild-build-pipeline|0.99|1|2026-07-30T05:01:48.315Z
  4d839c4e|knowledge|npm-dependencies|Dependencies: @inquirer/prompts (interactive prompts for CLI), @modelcontextprotocol/server (MCP SDK v2 beta), @toon-format/toon (TOON file format parser/serializer), zod (schema validation). Dev deps: typescript 7, vitest 4, esbuild, gpt-tokenizer. No runtime LLM dependency, no external services. Zero external service architecture keeps memory fully offline.|package.json|dependencies;package;npm;offline|2026-07-28||1|zero-deps-philosophy memory-io-layer esbuild-build-pipeline|1.00|1|2026-07-29T13:11:26.189Z
  f0276695|knowledge|typescript-configuration|TypeScript configuration in tsconfig.json: target ES2022, module NodeNext, strict mode enabled. Type-checks src/ directory only (excludes tests via exclude pattern). Includes 'declaration: true' for type generation. moduleResolution uses NodeNext for ESM compatibility. Uses Node types via @types/node. Runs in CI via 'npx tsc --noEmit' (not an npm script, run manually).|tsconfig.json|typescript;config;typecheck;tsconfig|2026-07-28||2|jsonl-format vitest-test-infrastructure esbuild-build-pipeline|0.99|1|2026-08-01T03:59:22.587Z
  7c3bbbfd|knowledge|vitest-test-infrastructure|Test infrastructure uses Vitest 4 with vitest.config.ts configuration. Tests are in tests/ directory. 16 test files with 278 tests total. Runs on Node 20/22 in CI. Each test uses temp directories and cleans up automatically. No external services required. Key test files: cli.test.ts (CLI integration), mcp-integration.test.ts (all MCP tools end-to-end), graph.test.ts, quality.test.ts, context.test.ts.|vitest.config.ts|test;vitest;ci;integration|2026-07-28||1|test-no-external test-temp-dirs test-auto-cleanup|0.99|1|2026-07-30T05:01:48.315Z
  edcd695c|knowledge|esbuild-build-pipeline|Build pipeline in package.json: 'npm run build' runs three esbuild steps sequentially via &&. First builds bin/toon-memory.js (entry: src/bin/toon-memory.ts, bundle: true, platform: node, target: node20, external: ['esbuild']). Second builds mcp/server.js (entry: src/mcp/server.ts, bundle with version injection via --define). Third builds dist/cli/*.js (4 files: setup.ts, opencode-plugin.ts, capture.ts, session-start.ts, external: all packages).|package.json|build;esbuild;pipeline;bundling|2026-07-28||2|esbuild-bundle viewer-html-generation build-output-layout|0.99|1|2026-07-30T05:01:48.315Z
  b60187d6|pattern|near-duplicate-detection|Near-duplicate detection in consolidation uses Jaccard similarity on word sets. Two entries are considered near-duplicates if Jaccard > 0.5 (50% word overlap). mergeSimilar() in consolidation.ts scans all entries pairwise (O(n²)) and merges matching pairs by keeping the longer content and combining tags. Runs on demand via memory_merge_similar or memory_consolidate.|src/mcp/consolidation.ts|dedup;jaccard;similarity;merge;consolidation|2026-07-28||1|consolidation-algorithm fuzzy-search-module opencode-plugin-auto-loading|0.99|1|2026-07-29T13:13:16.399Z
  47292af9|pattern|bm25-search-ranking|BM25 ranking in src/lib/graph.ts implements the Okapi BM25 algorithm for text search. Parameters: k1=1.5 (term saturation), b=0.75 (length normalization). Tokenization splits on whitespace and camelCase. Structural boosting: Functions/Methods +10, Routes +8, Classes/Interfaces +5. Noise labels (File/Folder/Module/Variable) excluded from results. avgDocLen computed from all entries.|src/lib/graph.ts|bm25;search;ranking;ir;tokenization|2026-07-28||1|bm25-ranking utils-module auto-linking-depth|1.00|1|2026-07-30T16:13:07.557Z
  49ec9452|pattern|quality-scoring-pattern|Quality scoring in src/lib/quality.ts calculates 0-1 scores based on: tags (bonus for 1-5 tags), links (bonus for 1-5 links), content length (optimal 50-500 chars), recency (1.0 fresh, decays to 0.2 over 365 days), specificity (detecting code, paths, URLs, numbers), access frequency (more accesses = higher), staleness decay (-0.2 after 30 days no access). Combined via weighted product.|src/lib/quality.ts|quality;scoring;decay;staleness;recency|2026-07-28||0|quality-score-formula quality-staleness-decay quality-scoring|0.99|1|
  e77b6256|pattern|observation-auto-prune|Observations auto-prune at 500 entries to prevent bloat. When a new observation pushes the count over 500, the oldest entries are removed. Pruning happens on write, not on a timer. Observations are stored in observations.toon with tool name, file, and timestamp. This keeps the capture log manageable while retaining recent context.|src/cli/hooks.ts|observations;prune;auto;capture;bloat|2026-07-28||0|capture-hook-architecture backup-rotation-pattern opencode-plugin-auto-loading|0.99|1|
  25021ec0|pattern|session-pruning-pattern|Session pruning removes stale sessions (older than 7 days or with expired TTL). pruneSessions() in src/lib/sessions.ts scans the sessions directory, checks each session's last-seen timestamp, and deletes stale ones. Runs on MCP server startup and periodically. Prevents build-up of orphan session files from disconnected agents.|src/lib/sessions.ts|session;pruning;stale;cleanup|2026-07-28||1|file-locking-pattern session-start-hook resources-registration|0.99|1|2026-07-30T16:13:07.203Z
  06772376|pattern|token-efficient-context|Context generation tools use token-efficient patterns: compact mode (only signatures, no full source) for context_brief, rebuild mode (hierarchical with token budgets) for context_generate. Truncation detection via comparing total_results to limit. All context_* tools return structured data without LLM processing - pure deterministic logic from memory data.|src/lib/context.ts|context;tokens;efficiency;compact|2026-07-28||3|context-rebuild-hierarchical graph-recall-algorithm opencode-plugin-auto-loading|0.99|1|2026-07-29T13:13:30.218Z
  652f03b9|pattern|backup-rotation-pattern|Backup system keeps the last 10 timestamped backups in .toon-memory/memory/backups/. Each backup file includes the date in the filename (e.g. memory-2026-07-28T16-00-00.toon). Older backups beyond the 10 limit are automatically pruned. Used by memory_backup tool and triggered before major operations like archive or consolidation.|src/mcp/tools.ts|backup;rotation;pruning;safety|2026-07-29||1|commands-module file-locking-pattern config-module|1.00|1|2026-07-29T13:11:06.342Z
  42497e1c|pattern|zod-schema-validation|All MCP tool parameters use Zod schemas for validation. Each tool defines its input schema using z.object() with typed fields, optional defaults, and descriptive messages. Schemas include string/number/boolean with min/max constraints. Enums for categories (decision, pattern, bug, knowledge, architecture) and modes (flat, graph, rebuild).|src/mcp/tools.ts|zod;validation;schemas;typescript|2026-07-28||0|mcp-tool-error-handling tool-error-handling agents-module|0.99|1|
  2f34b1f0|pattern|file-locking-pattern|File locking in src/lib/lock.ts prevents concurrent access to .toon files. Uses a lock file (.toon-memory/memory/.lock) with PID and timestamp. acquireLock() creates the lock file atomically, releaseLock() removes it. Times out after 5 seconds if lock cannot be acquired. Used by readMemory() and writeMemory() to prevent corruption from parallel agent sessions.|src/lib/lock.ts|locking;concurrency;file;atomic|2026-07-28||1|session-start-hook capture-hook-architecture config-writer-architecture|0.99|1|2026-07-29T13:11:26.189Z
  819ccdd9|pattern|mcp-tool-error-handling|MCP tools use try/catch with error messages returned as content responses, not thrown exceptions. Each tool wraps its logic in try/catch and returns { isError: true, content: [{ type: 'text', text: error.message }] }. This ensures the MCP server never crashes on user errors. Input validation uses Zod schemas before processing.|src/mcp/tools.ts|error-handling;mcp;robustness;validation|2026-07-28||0|tool-error-handling memory-io-layer crypto-module|1.00|1|
  142fad85|architecture|config-module|Config module in src/mcp/config.ts handles configuration loading, key management, and limits. loadConfig() reads .toon-memory/memory/config.json. MAX_ENTRIES constant (default 100) triggers archive warnings. Key management for encryption mode. Config includes file paths for data.toon, archive.toon, observations.toon, and session storage directories.|src/mcp/config.ts|config;limits;paths;keys|2026-07-28||0|fuzzy-search-module entries-module synonyms-module|0.99|1|
