  05f7ee8b|architecture|entries-module|Entries module in src/mcp/entries.ts provides entry management utilities: generateId() creates unique entry IDs using timestamp + random, parseTTL() converts TTL strings (e.g. '7d', '2026-07-17') to dates, isExpired() checks TTL expiration, inferTags() auto-tags content by keyword matching (verbatim mode skips this), parseRelativeDate() handles relative date strings for date filtering.|src/mcp/entries.ts|entries;id;ttl;tags;parsing|2026-07-28||0|archive-module toon-v1-format synonyms-module|0.99|1|
  2ca23a3a|architecture|crypto-module|Crypto module in src/mcp/crypto.ts implements AES-256-GCM encryption for memory data. encrypt(data, key) returns base64-encoded ciphertext with IV prepended. decrypt(ciphertext, key) reverses the process. Key derivation uses PBKDF2 with salt. The TOON_MEMORY_KEY environment variable supplies the encryption key. Encryption is opt-in via memory_encrypt tool.|src/mcp/crypto.ts|crypto;aes;gcm;encryption;security|2026-07-28||0|security-env-keys aes256gcm-encrypt encrypt-decrypt|0.99|1|
  06a19b17|architecture|synonyms-module|Synonyms module in src/lib/synonyms.ts provides term expansion for improved memory recall. Maps common terms to their synonyms (e.g. 'config' ↔ 'configuration', 'delete' ↔ 'remove' ↔ 'forget'). Used during smart_recall to broaden search queries and find entries that use different terminology. Domain-specific synonym maps for memory system terminology.|src/lib/synonyms.ts|synonyms;search;recall;nlp|2026-07-28||0|fuzzy-search-module commands-module resources-registration|0.98|1|
  0ddf30db|architecture|fuzzy-search-module|Fuzzy search in src/lib/fuzzy.ts implements approximate string matching for memory recall. Uses Levenshtein distance with configurable threshold. Falls back gracefully when no fuzzy matches are found. Integrated into graph recall and smart recall for broader matching when exact keyword search misses relevant entries.|src/lib/fuzzy.ts|fuzzy;search;levenshtein;matching|2026-07-28||0|viewer-keyboard-shortcuts memory-io-layer opencode-plugin-auto-loading|0.99|1|
  110252b3|architecture|commands-module|Commands module in src/cli/commands.ts provides the core CLI command implementations. Includes initProject() to set up the .toon-memory directory structure, showStatus() for current state, showStats() with category breakdowns, exportToon()/importToon() for data portability, watchMemory() for file watching, upgradeSelf() for self-update, and uninstallSelf() for cleanup.|src/cli/commands.ts|cli;commands;init;export;import;watch|2026-07-28||0|cli-setup-routing cli-commands session-start-hook|0.99|1|
  2f1ea9a7|architecture|agents-module|Agents module in src/cli/agents.ts detects which AI coding agent is running and installs the appropriate capture hooks. Supports 15+ agents: OpenCode, Claude, Cursor, Continue, Gemini, Codex, Kiro, Mimocode, Cline, Impeccable, Windsurf, CodeGPT, Codium, Aider, Augment, Copilot. Detection is by environment variables, config file presence, or process arguments. Each agent gets a tailored config with tool_use captures.|src/cli/agents.ts|agents;detection;hooks;integration|2026-07-28||0|config-writer-architecture 15-agents cli-setup-routing|0.99|1|
