  8ad67378|architecture|viewer-keyboard-shortcuts|Viewer keyboard shortcuts: / focuses search, Escape clears search or deselects entry and switches to graph tab, 1-4 switches tabs (Graph/Stats/Timeline/Detail). When input is focused, Escape only clears and blurs the input. All shortcuts ignore input elements except the Escape+blur behavior.|src/viewer/html.ts|viewer;keyboard;ux;shortcuts|2026-07-29||1|viewer-theme-toggle viewer-standalone viewer-html-generation|1.00|1|2026-07-29T13:11:06.342Z
  6d40a55a|architecture|viewer-export-features|Viewer supports PNG and SVG export. PNG uses Canvas 2D: serializes the SVG element to XML, converts to base64 data URL, loads it into an Image, draws to a 2x resolution canvas, then exports via link download. SVG export directly serializes the SVG to a Blob and creates an object URL. Both handle the dark/light background via getComputedStyle.|src/viewer/html.ts|viewer;export;png;svg;canvas|2026-07-29||1|viewer-export-png viewer-standalone d3-graph-viewer|1.00|1|2026-07-29T13:12:06.257Z
  39f1e7b4|architecture|viewer-force-graph|Viewer graph uses D3 forceSimulation with 4 forces: link (distance-based), charge (many-body repulsion, default -120), center (gravity to center, default 0.05), collision (radius-based). Nodes are circle elements, edges are line elements. The simulation runs on tick to update positions. Nodes are draggable (fixes position on drag), right-click to unfix. Minimap shows a scaled-down overview with its own SVG.|src/viewer/html.ts|viewer;d3js;force-graph;simulation;physics|2026-07-29||0|graph-minimap-render graph-force-layout graph-physics-controls|0.99|1|
